testcase.system-out:
@scenario.begin
@clock @time @tick Scenario: Time label updates every second Given the system time is 12:00:05 ... passed in 0.005s And the active app is "Clock" ... passed in 0.001s When one second elapses ... passed in 0.001s Then the clock shows time "12:00:06" ... passed in 0.001s When one more second elapses ... passed in 0.000s Then the clock shows time "12:00:07" ... passed in 0.000s
@scenario.end --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@scenario.begin
@clock @date @minute Scenario: Date label updates when minute changes Given the detailed system time is Monday 2025-09-29 12:34:55 ... passed in 0.001s And the active app is "Clock" ... passed in 0.001s And the date label is currently hidden ... passed in 0.000s When 10 seconds elapse ... passed in 0.000s And one more second elapses (minute rollover) ... passed in 0.000s Then the date label text becomes "Mon 29 Sep" ... passed in 0.000s
@scenario.end --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@scenario.begin

  @clock @format @encoder
  Scenario: Rotating encoder LEFT toggles format
    Given the system time is 21:09:59 ... passed in 0.000s
    And the active app is "Clock" ... passed in 0.001s
    And the clock format is 24h ... passed in 0.000s
    When I rotate LEFT on the encoder ... passed in 0.001s
    Then the clock shows time "09:09:59" ... passed in 0.000s

@scenario.end
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@scenario.begin
@clock @date @popup Scenario: Encoder RIGHT shows date for 3 seconds then hides Given the detailed system time is Tuesday 2025-09-30 08:15:10 ... passed in 0.001s And the active app is "Clock" ... passed in 0.001s And the date label is hidden ... passed in 0.001s When I rotate RIGHT on the encoder ... passed in 0.000s Then the date label is visible ... passed in 0.000s When 2 seconds elapse ... passed in 0.001s Then the date label is still visible ... passed in 0.000s When 1 more second elapses ... passed in 0.001s Then the date label is hidden again ... passed in 0.000s
@scenario.end --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@scenario.begin
@clock @power @wip Scenario: Clock stops updating when device is IDLE Given the system time is 10:00:00 ... passed in 0.000s And the active app is "Clock" ... passed in 0.000s And the device enters IDLE power state ... failed in 0.004s When 5 seconds elapse ... skipped in 0.000s Then the clock still shows time "10:00:00" ... skipped in 0.000s When the device returns to ACTIVE ... skipped in 0.000s And one second elapses ... skipped in 0.000s Then the clock shows time "10:00:01" ... skipped in 0.000s
@scenario.end --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@scenario.begin

  @clock @sync @wip
  Scenario: Time jump causes immediate display update
    Given the system time is 11:59:58 ... passed in 0.001s
    And the active app is "Clock" ... passed in 0.001s
    When the system time jumps to 12:10:00 ... passed in 0.001s
    Then the clock shows time "12:10:00" ... passed in 0.000s

@scenario.end
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@scenario.begin
@clock @display @cycle Scenario: Tap cycles display type forward Given the system time is 12:00:00 ... passed in 0.000s And the active app is "Clock" ... passed in 0.001s And the display type is Digital ... passed in 0.000s When I tap the clock display ... passed in 0.001s Then the display type is Analogue ... passed in 0.000s When I tap the clock display ... passed in 0.000s Then the display type is Nixie ... passed in 0.000s When I tap the clock display ... passed in 0.000s Then the display type is Digital ... passed in 0.000s
@scenario.end --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@scenario.begin

  @clock @display @wip
  Scenario: Display type persists across restart (future)
    Given the display type is Nixie ... passed in 0.000s
    And the app is restarted ... passed in 0.001s
    Then the display type is Nixie ... passed in 0.001s

@scenario.end
